Banking Backend System

📌 Overview

This project is a backend banking system built using Spring Boot and Java Persistence API (JPA). It focuses on designing a scalable and structured data model to manage core banking operations such as customers, accounts, and transactions.

The application demonstrates how real-world financial systems organize and persist data using Object Relational Mapping (ORM).

🛠️ Technologies Used
Java
Spring Boot
JPA (Java Persistence API)
Hibernate
Maven

💼 Use Case

This project simulates a simplified banking system backend, which can be extended into a full-stack financial application with APIs and frontend integration.

⭐ Acknowledgment

This project was built as part of a hands-on learning experience to understand real-world backend development and enterprise-level application structure.
